    "allowed_sports_note": "The sports Today Match and Upcoming may publish, and the last gate they pass through: scanner/events.py _payload drops any card whose sport_type is not in this list. It named thirteen sports while two were ever published, which read as a policy nobody was enforcing. It is not redundant with scanner/sport_filter.py - the filter decides what a fixture IS from its own evidence and stamps sport_type accordingly, and this says which of those may reach a tab. Narrowing it changed nothing on the day it was measured: every one of the 282 published cards was already cricket or football, and the filter only ever keeps those two.",
    "provider_event_hours_note": "The generic assumed fallback for when a fixture ends - nothing more. The name says provider and no provider states this: it is kickoff + these hours, computed here, and end_time_source records it as 'assumed' so no downstream rule mistakes it for evidence. It is reached only after both better answers fail: a provider that stated an end (end_time_source 'provider') and a sport whose length is known (sport). Measured on a real scan of 282 published cards: sport 194, assumed 83, provider 5 - and 65 of the assumed ones end exactly four hours after kickoff, which is this setting. Still load-bearing, so the value is unchanged."
